      "markdown": "\n<table border=1 style='margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;'><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>主句</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>从句</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'></td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>unless+</td></tr></table>\n\n\n<table border=1 style='margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;'><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>主句</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>从句</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>一般将来时</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>unless + 一般现在时</td></tr></table>\n\n## Grammar Summary 4, page 119\n\n $ \\Leftrightarrow $语法总结4, 第119页。\n\n1 meet 2 feel 一般现在时 3 try 4 relax 一般将来时,一般现在时\n\n## 教材问题答案\n\n7 Complete the sentences with the correct form of the verbs in brackets.\n\n1 If you ___ (not understand), ___ (ask) your teacher.\n\n2 She ___ (not be) satisfied unless her son ___ (win) first place.\n\n3 If you ___ (see) a red light, ___ (not cross) the road.\n\n4 You ___ (not feel) relaxed unless you ___ (learn) to let go.\n\n如果你___ (不理解)，___ (问)\n\n你的老师。\n\n\n\n用括号中动词的正确形式完成句子。\n\n她 ___ （不）满意，除非她儿子 ___ （赢得）第一。\n\n如果你___（看到）红灯，___（不要过）马路。\n\n你 ___ (不觉得)放松,除非你 ___\n\n(学会)放手。\n\nI don't understand, ask  2 won't be, wins  3 see, don't cross  4 won't feel, learn\n\n## Speaking\n\n8 Role-play Role-play a conversation with your friend. Use the expressions below and ideas from the box or your own ideas.\n\n## 说\n\n角色扮演 和你的朋友分角色对话。要使用下面的表达及方框中的观点或者你自己的想法。\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"imgs/img_in_image_box_468_7450_818_7835.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" width=\"4%\" /></div>\n\n\nI had a quarrel/ $ k\\check{w} $r $ \\underline{a} $l/ with my best friend $ ^{19} $ and I'm feeling really down. What should I do?\n\n我和我最好的朋友吵了一架,我觉得\n\n情绪很低落。我该怎么办?\n\n\n\nlearn to forgive/fə'grv/ and forget, talk to him/her, say you're sorry, tell him/her your feelings, write him/her a sorry note\n\n• If you've said something impolite/mpə'laɪt/²⁰,...\n\n• Your friend won't understand unless...\n\n• If you want to make up with your friend,...\n\n• You won't feel better unless...\n\n## Example\n\nIf you've said something impolite, say sorry to your friend.\n\n学会原谅和忘记,和他 / 她谈一谈,说你很抱歉,告诉他 / 她你的感受,给他 / 她写一张道歉便条\n\n\n\n如果你说了不礼貌的话，……\n\n你的朋友不会理解,除非……\n\n如果你想和你的朋友和好，……\n\n你不会感觉好点儿,除非……\n\n## 例子\n\n如果你说了不礼貌的话,向你的朋友道歉。",
